  "query_preview": "..\nIssued at 233 PM EST Sun Nov 1 2026\n\n- Small rain chances through Tue; Rain Likely Tue night/Wed\n\nAnother day of mostly cloud cover for the area today. Regional radar \nimagery looks a bit more ominous than reality with a short wave \nmoving through. This is the case with plenty of echoes present, but \nclouds below 10k ft are few and far between. We will see the short \nwave move out tonight, and short wave and long wave ridging will \nbuild over the area.\n\nMonday will see another day with plenty of cloud cover as low level \nand upper level moisture moves in. Forecast soundings and moisture X-\nsections indicate a lack of clouds/moisture in the mid levels with \nabout a 6-8k dry layer in between. Can not rule out a sprinkle, but \nthere is really no forcing most of the day. We do see a better low \nlevel jet set up late in the day and Monday night that will be \nfocused on the northern portion of the forecast area. This will \nresult in some showers for Central Lower.\n\nMost of Tuesday will be mostly dry across the area. We see the \nshowers Monday move to the north, and we will be waiting for the \nmoisture axis ahead of the incoming long wave trough and cold front. \nAnother period of ridging will be in place most of the day, with the \narea in the warm sector. 850 mb temps of around +13C will support \nhighs in the 70s once again.\n\nThe best chance of rain with this entire system will come overnight \nTuesday night into Wednesday. We see the nose of a 50 knots low \nlevel jet set its sights on the forecast area. In addition to the \nrain, there looks to be just a enough instability for a rumble of \nthunder late Tuesday night/Wednesday morning just ahead of the \nfront. Sfc based and elevated lifted indices are slightly negative \nat this time. The front will move through mostly by dark Wednesday \nevening.  \n\n- Cooler with rain chances Thu-Fri\n\nWe will see a break in the rain chances Wednesday night behind the \ncold front as we end up under the dry slot. This will cool off the \ntemperatures a bit too, but not significantly yet. The upper low \nwill settle over the area by Thursday, bringing with it better deep \nlayer instability and cyclonic flow along with short waves. This \nwill bring showery weather off and on for Thursday and much of \nFriday, with highs dropping back into the 50s. Lake effect rain \nshowers will also be possible with 850 mb temps dropping to almost \n0C, bringing delta t's to the mid teens C. \n\n- Dry Saturday with rain chances increasing Sun\n\nThe upper jet core will shift out of the area Friday evening, \nbringing anti-cyclonic flow back to the area. The showers should \ntaper off as the colder air aloft also moves out of the area. We are \nlooking at a dry and cool day on Saturday right now as ridging \nbuilding in. There is pretty good agreement that another short wave \nwill be diving down from the NW on Sunday, bringing more chances for \nrain to the region, and reinforcing colder air.",
